{
  "dom_id": "step-q96429",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{2-2{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{2-2{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{1-{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}-2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{0}-1}{{e}^{0}+1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{2}-1}{{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
